    SC001["<div class='arg'><b>SC001 · Scenario · Fed does not hike in September</b><div class='c sup'><span><b>IF:</b> The Fed does not hike with current pricing.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The Fed risks a sharp and disorderly UST long end move.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> US 30Y rapidly tests 5.75%.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> A larger market move comes from a Fed hold.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> There is a material front end rate decline.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> There is a sharp twist steepening of the curve.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> Total hikes decline to 65-75bps.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> Hikes by end '26 decline to 30-35bps.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> Initially, 2Y is lower by 15-20bps.</span><b>[S]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> Initially, the 30Y bond increases 10-15bps.</span><b>[S]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>THEN:</b> Over time, the 30Y increases towards 5.75%.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> Investor confidence in the Fed is limited.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> Treasury buybacks prove futile to stop the UST long end move.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The Fed hold represents an unprecedented dovish hold (using FOMC OIS data back to '07).</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>THEN:</b> The dollar depreciates swiftly and significantly.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
